  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Connecticut has received $19B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $18.6B of that total. Contract activity in Connecticut includes 26,372 awards with an average award size of $722K. Obligations fell 45.8% year over year. The current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress. Engineering Services accounts for $7B in obligations and Ship Building and Repairing accounts for $4.4B. ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION received $11.3B in obligations, making it the largest vendor by dollar value in the state. Recent fiscal year totals show variation: FY21 was $18.4B, FY22 was $22.3B, FY23 was $26B, FY24 was $20B, FY25 was $35.1B, and FY26 is $19B. These figures reflect contract obligations only and the picture is dominated by Defense spending and ship and aircraft-related industries.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are the biggest buyers in Connecticut?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $18.6B in obligations. The Department of Homeland Security follows with $181M, and the Department of Veterans Affairs follows with $116M. Civilian agencies together account for the remaining, smaller obligations listed."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top contractors and what industries get the most?",
        "body": "ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION is the top contractor with $11.3B in obligations. RTX CORPORATION and SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION follow with $3.8B and $2.8B respectively. Engineering Services, Ship Building and Repairing, and Aircraft Manufacturing lead industries with $7B, $4.4B, and $3.2B respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
